            "message": "Done. Here's what I built in `erp-api/`:\n\n**Order Management API** (`/api/orders`):\n- `POST` create orders with multi-platform source, item details, shipping address\n- `GET` list with platform/status/date filtering + pagination\n- `GET :id` order details\n- `PUT :id/status` status updates with state machine enforcement\n\n**Inventory Sync API** (`/api/inventory`):\n- `GET /sync` triggers multi-platform sync with a distributed lock (prevents concurrent syncs)\n- `GET :sku` queries inventory across all platforms\n- `PUT :sku` updates stock with distributed lock + negative quantity protection\n\n**Key design choices**: Zod validation on every endpoint, Redis distributed locks to prevent overselling, platform adapter pattern for sync extensibility, JSONB for flexible item storage, and state machine for order status transitions.\n\nThe architect and QA should review — architect for alignment with planned architecture, QA for testing all endpoints including concurrency and edge cases.",
